cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying master's thesis."
title: "V2Guard: Privacy-Preserving Blockchain-Driven Intrusion Detection for Vehicle-to-Grid Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Azedine
    given-names: Hamza
  - family-names: Bourouis
    given-names: Adam
year: 2025
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Azzeddinehamza/v2guard-federated-blockchain-ids"
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - blockchain
  - intrusion detection
  - vehicle-to-grid
  - cyber-physical systems security
  - privacy
abstract: >-
  Federated intrusion detection framework for Vehicle-to-Grid networks in which
  model updates are anchored as hashes in a Solidity smart contract and verified
  before aggregation. Evaluated with Random Forest and DNN models on NSL-KDD and
  UNSW-NB15 across six non-IID clients.
